/// Checks canonical point encodings (A's, then R's, by one loop running the decoding twice) and S < L, then evaluates the uncofactored equation using all 512 challenge bits. Computes [k]A - [S]B with one chain of doublings and 4-bit windows of the public scalars, from a table of [1]A to [15]A and constant -[1]B to -[15]B, skipping the leading zero bytes of k above its low 32, and compares it with -R projectively. Point tables and callee-saved registers reside in `scratch`; field products call `vg_gf25519_r32_mul`.
///
